  description: Captured DMG 53256–53257 distinguish disqualification from the initial suspension of
    ESA(Cont) payment and the retrospective first-day decision. DMG 53258 and 42580 treat the
    claimant as not having limited capability for work if disqualification exceeds six weeks; 41823
    says these are not days of entitlement. DMG 41832 retains cases of continuing entitlement while
    not payable, expressly subject to the six-week qualification and other termination conditions.
    No-penalty, hospital, fine-default and overseas branches at 53259–53287 prevent a universal
    rule; a person not disqualified may still have payment suspended under 53284, subject to 53285.
